flowchart TD
  subgraph inputs["Authority inputs"]
    I1["S1-S4 sealed entity and graph world<br/>parties, accounts, instruments, devices, IPs, and links"]
    I2["Fraud-role priors, taxonomy, and validation policy<br/>the only lawful surfaces for static posture and closure"]
  end

  subgraph core["Actual S5 design"]
    C1["Assign static fraud posture across the closed graph world<br/>party, account, merchant, device, and IP roles"]
    C2["Validate the entire 6A world as a segment<br/>consistency of bases, links, roles, and contract surfaces"]
    C3["Assemble the 6A validation bundle and HashGate<br/>the closure signal that 6B must trust"]
  end

  subgraph shifts["Implemented design shifts"]
    S1["The actual implementation abandoned heavy graph-scoring ambitions here<br/>static fraud posture became deterministic hash-based role assignment over sealed priors and existing features"]
    S2["Prior-role ids and contracted taxonomy ids had to be explicitly mapped<br/>so S5 judged the same role language the rest of the engine reads"]
    S3["Bundle construction stayed intentionally light<br/>reports and issue tables were bundled, while large role tables stayed in egress and were referenced by closure rather than recopied"]
  end

